  "description": "Gamechanger Audio Bigsby Pedal: every controller of its CC map, the MSB and LSB pairs as 14-bit values.",
  "sources": [
    {
      "type": "manual",
      "title": "Bigsby Pedal CC & PC map",
      "notes": "The CC map (PDF page 1), read by tools/profiles/gamechanger/read-pedal-cc.mjs from BIGSBY-MANUAL-CC-PC-MAP-desktop-read.pdf (sha256 b465698064bc90555334ee0ce75ccc52d8e19054f7ba06126bb45456ccefc604), https://gamechangeraudio.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/BIGSBY-MANUAL-CC-PC-MAP-desktop-read.pdf, linked from https://gamechangeraudio.com/downloads/. Not yet checked against the pedal itself."
    }
  ],
  "testedWith": [],
  "authoringNotes": [
    "Generated by tools/profiles/gamechanger/make-profiles.mjs; edit the layout in tools/profiles/gamechanger/synths/, not this file.",
    "Every parameter is a row of the document's CC map, on the channel variable; an MSB row and the LSB row 32 above it are one 14-bit value, the MSB sent first. Nothing here has been sent to a real pedal yet.",
    "The map sets the pedal's position three ways: CC 27 in 7 bits, CC 28 and 60 in 14, and the pitch wheel; and the EXP output's override value two (CC 105, CC 26 and 58). Each is laid out as printed. Its program changes (loading and saving the ten preset slots, the pitch ranges, the EXP override and more) are not laid out."
  ],
